25-26-468267","filed":"2026-11-19","form":"10-K","id":"US-WWD","model":"gemini-3.6-flash","name":"Woodward, Inc.","offered":3,"period":"2026-09-30","points":[{"point":"Woodward expects a future annuity buyout to trigger a noncash pension settlement charge against accumulated components in other comprehensive income.","quote":"The Company anticipates an annuity purchase or a “buy-out” will likely occur within the next fiscal year or shortly thereafter, which will trigger a pension settlement that will result in all plan balances, including accumulated pension components within other comprehensive income, being charged to expense as a noncash settlement charge.","topic":"accounting"},{"point":"Woodward approved transitioning production from Santa Clarita and expects additional restructuring expenses of $34,000 to $44,000 through late 2027.","quote":"The Company anticipates these additional expenses, which are expected to be approximately $ 34,000 to $ 44,000 in total, will be substantially complete by the end of calendar year 2027.","topic":"other"},{"point":"Woodward approved a plan to wind down its on-highway natural gas truck manufacturing operations in China following unsuccessful divestment efforts.","quote":"On January 12, 2026, the Company approved a plan to wind down its on-highway natural gas truck manufacturing operations in China (the “China OH Business”).","topic":"other"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/108312/000119312526468267/wwd-20260930.htm"},"tone":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,nul